Consider the following iterative Binary Search implementation for a sorted array `arr` of size `n`:

```java
int low = 0, high = n - 1;
while (low <= high) {
    int mid = low + (high - low) / 2;
    if (arr[mid] == target) return mid;
    else if (arr[mid] > target) {
        high = mid; // Line X
    } else {
        low = mid + 1;
    }
}
return -1;
```

What is the primary consequence of the update `high = mid` in Line X when the target is not present in the array?
